# Open eiConsole (Mac)

When the user asks to open eiConsole (e.g. "open the eiConsole", "launch eiConsole"), do it — do not only give instructions.

## Resolve working directory

Prefer the **active interface** `eip-root` (folder containing `interfaces/`):

1. Path the user names or `@`-mentions
2. Else nearest `…/eip-root` from open/recent files, chat context, or cwd under `Clients/**`
3. Else ask which interface if several are plausible

Valid WD: absolute path to that `eip-root` with an `interfaces` directory.

If none can be determined → launch eiConsole **without** changing prefs.

## Launch (Mac)

App: `/Applications/eiConsole/eiConsole.app` (prefer this over guinea installs).

When WD is known:

1. Write `com.pilotfish.eip.console.workingDirectory_0` in `~/Library/Preferences/com.pilotfish.eip.plist` (nested `/com/pilotfish/eip/` → `gui/` → `console/` → `config/` → `prefs/`) to the eip-root path
2. Rotate that path to index 0 among existing `workingDirectory_*` (dedupe; keep ~10)
3. If eiConsole is already running, quit it so prefs reload
4. `open -a "/Applications/eiConsole/eiConsole.app"`

When WD is unknown: only step 4.

Confirm briefly with the path used, or that none was set.
